Z||000000||dogtired||08-27-2000||01:34 AM||||Anyone out here into lead melting and casting toys? I have melted wheel weights for years and have several molds, Toy soldiers and a cool cannon. Anyone else?<BR>If anyone has any molds from fishing sinkers to toys I would be interested.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000001||Phil||08-27-2000||07:35 AM||||Used to cast bullets,just make sure you stay away from melting down car batteries (real nasty fumes). Seeing that you're using wheel weights did you know that you can heat treat that alloy and double the hardness?||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||08-27-2000||02:30 PM||||I've done a little.... been years. Only lead I handle now is soldering. I try to use lead free solders when I can.<P>For anyone doing this......<P>Please use good masks to block lead vapor and gloves. Lead is skin absorbed as I remember, even if it's not you'll likely rub it into your face or something w/o thinking about it. ((Some alloys and lead compounds are more skin absorbed than others. The lead compound that used to be in gasoline was especially bad.))<P>Never melt lead based batteries. They give off nasty lead and other toxic compounds in those horrid smelling fumes.<P>Don't do it in the house. The lead vapor can contaminate every surface in the place. Children are especially suseptable to this contamination because of their toys etc....<P>The EPA and OSHA are really picky about lead handling these days. If you get caught disposing of lead w/o proper containment it's big fines. Same thing with OSHA and use of lead in the workplace. (You should see the rules for soldering stations now....)||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||08-27-2000||04:17 PM||||Geez Ogre, what other obscure facts do you have for us?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  What do you do in your spare time!?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||08-28-2000||12:58 PM||||Please let me take ths opportunity to applaud Ogre. I've been meaning to send him e-mail, but I'm just gonna do it here. <P>If you've ever read anything in Ogre's cave, you have probably noticed that there is one underlying thread that never changes. <BR>Safety. <P>I, for one, really appreciate this. <BR>I used to work for a company that didn't stress safety.<BR>As an indirect result of that (and as a direct result of my own carelessness), I was nearly electrocuted. Let me tell ya' 1500 VDC hurts like hell.<P>I know this is a different situation, but injuries can happen in any number of ways. <BR>Not to detract from any of the other posts, but thanks, Ogre.<P>Just be careful, guys. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>When I die, I want to go peacefully, in my sleep, like Grandpa.<BR>Not screaming, like the passengers in his car.||||reg||14
Z||000005||theogre||08-28-2000||11:48 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Your welcome..... It's a hold over from working at DuPont for a year or 2. They were perfectly anal about it. (That's also where I found out just how nasty Tetra Ethyl Lead, the stuff used in gasoline, really was. They used to make it in the plant on the NJ side of the delaware bridge. Nasty nasty stuff. Took years to clean up. Not sure they've finished yet.)||||reg||1
