Z||000007||Monkeyman||08-29-2000||12:40 AM||||In all seriousness, lead <I>is</I> a bad thing to mess with.  We had problems getting our mortgage approved because we couldn't prove that the original lead based paint was completely removed.  Leads to birth defects and looooong lasting illnesses.  <P>dog (and others)--Be very careful.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Patrick||08-29-2000||03:45 AM||||<BR>This is a little off the topic, but I remember years ago (back in '67) we had a "home made" thermometer sitting in our grade six science class for weeks (months?). It was simply an open bowl of <B><I>mercury</I></B> with a glass tube standing up in it. As if breathing the vapour from that mercury for weeks wasn't bad enough, <B>we were actually encouraged by the teacher to play with the damn mercury with our bare hands!!!</B> I cringe when I think about it now. I sometimes wonder whether or not there was a higher percentage of birth defects to kids born from my long ago classmates. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000009||Phil||08-29-2000||07:50 AM||||Elemental mercury isn't the real nasty stuff  the salts of mercury  are, same thing for lead. You want safety stuff- I worked for an arsenal for awhile. Blood tests every month(checking for lead) EKG every 6 months. Buildings full of explosives all kinds of fun stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000010||dogtired||08-29-2000||05:36 PM||||OK so I brought up a TOXIC Topic  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Maybe that is why my parents let me have the lead melting set when I was 12 about 40 years ago???  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>I also have a couple piant containers of Mercury, Fun stuff to mess with but be very careful!! I understand a lot of Gold prospectors use mercury to help pick up gold flakes, during panning. Then the process is to burn the mercury away with a torch. Which leaves the GOLD, if you are still alive. The smoke from burning mercury is very, very TOXIC. :O This stuff is about as safe as trying to remove your engine cradle with one screw jack.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   Be CAREFUL out there Folks.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
